  "title": "Chapter 5: PERIODIC CLASSIFICATION OF ELEMENTS",
  "order": 25,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "0ax5340",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Need for Classification"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Dobereiner arranged elements with similar properties into groups of three called triads based on atomic mass.",
        "Newlands' Law of Octaves stated that every eighth element had properties similar to that of the first when arranged by atomic mass.",
        "Mendeleev formulated the Periodic Table based on atomic masses and successfully predicted undiscovered elements like Eka-Silicon (Germanium).",
        "Henry Moseley showed that atomic number, rather than atomic mass, is the fundamental property determining elemental characteristics.",
        "In the Modern Periodic Table, atomic size decreases across a period and increases down a group."
      ],
      "id": "1vltonz"
    },
